From f900071c6abff340d598ad7395bf2acd3ad929d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] ui.c: a held step's SEL list keeps SELECT from the lock
 editor

A step held and EDIT pressed opens the lock editor (ui.lockpg); SEL then
opens the step's list (REMOVE <note>, COPY STEP, CLEAR LOCKS). Every
SELECT turn was still taken by the lock editor's page cycle before the
list saw it, so the highlight never moved: the footer offers SELECT move
and nothing happens. ALGORITHM (list_change) and SEL (list_sel) kept
working, which is why only the move broke.

A list open over the lock editor now keeps SELECT for its rows; the
lock editor's page cycle resumes once the list closes (the held step and
EDIT are untouched, as they were).

tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy: the list opened over the lock editor,
SELECT down to CLEAR LOCKS, SEL picks it, the step's note stays (the
unfixed build picks REMOVE instead and the note is gone).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 app/ui.c                        |  3 ++-
 tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy

diff --git a/app/ui.c b/app/ui.c
index b4311e2..5276a7f 100644
--- a/app/ui.c
+++ b/app/ui.c
@@ -3511,7 +3511,8 @@ static void input(void)
         ui.act_t = plat_ms();
     if (ui.ask)
         return;
-    if ((e = ev[EN_SELECT]) != 0 && ui.lockpg) {  /* the lock editor: the module's other pages (the track's own) */
+    if ((e = ev[EN_SELECT]) != 0 && ui.lockpg && !lst.open) {   /* the lock editor: the module's other pages (the
+                                                  * track's own); a list open over it keeps SELECT for its rows */
         int g = page_group(ui.lockpg - 1), f = PAGE_BTN[g].first, n = group_n(g), pg = ui.lockpg - 1 - f;
         if (PAGE_BTN[g].btn == B_FX) {           /* the track's own: Character and Sends */
             f = P_CHARACTER;
diff --git a/tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy b/tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d21a896
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# A held step's SEL list, opened over the lock editor (step held + EDIT): SELECT moves its rows (not the lock
+# editor's pages), and SEL runs the row picked. With CLEAR LOCKS picked, the step's note stays.
+wait 300
+turn ALGO 1
+expect trk 2
+tap SEQ
+step 2 1 1 60 100
+key w0 down
+wait 60
+press EDIT
+wait 60
+tap SEL
+wait 60
+spin SELECT 2
+wait 60
+tap SEL
+wait 60
+expect note 2 1 1 60
+release EDIT
+key w0 up
